{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.crossVal_le_of_margin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.crossVal_le_of_margin","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/RelaxedVertexRounding.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**Rounding returns the integer optimum.**  Under the margin condition, the\nedge from `a` to the cheapest feasible word `b` is no more expensive than the\nedge to any other admissible feasible `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.slope_le_of_margin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.slope_le_of_margin","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/RelaxedVertexRounding.lean#L85-L102","doc":"**The margin condition.**  Let `b` be feasible with `c a < c b`, and let `j`\nbe any feasible word with `c j ≥ c b + δ` and `x j ≤ X`.  If\n`(c b − c a)(X − x b) ≤ δ (x b − x a)`, then `slope a b ≤ slope a j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.crossVal_le_iff_slope_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.crossVal_le_iff_slope_le","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/RelaxedVertexRounding.lean#L67-L83","doc":"**For a fixed infeasible `a`, a smaller slope means a cheaper mixture.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.mixture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.mixture","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/RelaxedVertexRounding.lean#L54-L65","doc":"The mixture weights: `λ = x b / (x b − x a)` on `a` lies in `(0, 1)`,\nkills the character, and has cost `crossVal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.crossVal_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.crossVal_eq","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/RelaxedVertexRounding.lean#L47-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.crossVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.crossVal","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/RelaxedVertexRounding.lean#L43-L44","doc":"Value of the mixture of `a` and `b` whose character is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.slope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.RelaxedVertexRounding.slope","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/RelaxedVertexRounding.lean#L40-L41","doc":"Slope of the cost against the character along the edge `a → b`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}